# Confirm / alert dialogs

Never use `window.confirm`, `window.alert`, or `window.prompt` in app UI.

Use `useAppConfirm()` instead:

```js
const { confirm, alert } = useAppConfirm()

const ok = await confirm({
  title: 'Delete source?',
  message: `Delete “${name}”? This cannot be undone.`,
  confirmLabel: 'Delete',
  danger: true,
})
if (!ok) return

await alert({ title: 'Saved', message: 'Changes were saved.' })
```

- Host is `AppConfirmDialog` in `app/app.vue` (z-index above full-screen editors).
- Prefer `danger: true` for destructive actions (Delete, Remove).
- Confirm handlers must be `async` when awaiting the dialog.
